## 4. Target logic (what to implement)

```text
open(workspace_id, slug, plane):
  tok = mint(plane, user)
  app = lookupApp(workspace, slug)   # from Coder API / agent apps

  if app.subdomain:
    host = f"{slug}--{workspaceName}--{username}.{wildcardBase(plane)}"
    // e.g. ttyd--alice-a--alice.coder-a.example.com
    target = url(scheme, host, port, path="/", query=…)
  else:
    target = f"{planeURL}/@{username}/{workspaceName}/apps/{slug}/"

  authStrategy(target, tok):
    // see §5
  302 → target
```

### Subdomain hostname format

Coder’s convention (as used in the subdomain lab):

```text
{app_slug}--{workspace_name}--{username}.{wildcard_without_star}
```

Example:

- Wildcard: `*.coder.127.0.0.1.sslip.io`
- App: `jupyter`, workspace `subdomlab`, user `alice`
- Host: `jupyter--subdomlab--alice.coder.127.0.0.1.sslip.io`

Confirm against your Coder version if names contain chars that get normalized.

### Looking up `subdomain`

Prefer reading from workspace/agent apps in the API response (each `coder_app` has sharing / subdomain metadata) rather than a static slug map. Fallback: config table `slug → mode` per template if API shape is awkward.

